s.save()

OR

s = Stuent.objects.create(name = ""..... ,)
if we create objects with thi scommand then we donot have to call .save() function

**********************************************

to take data from frontened to backend we have to add name parameter to the fields 
we have to add enctype = "multipart/form-data" in form tag if we are uploading files from frontend to backend
otherwise it will not work the image will not be uploaded to the backend

csrf token is used to protect the website from cross site request forgery attacks. it is a security measure to 
protect the website from malicious attacks. it is a token that is generated by the server and sent to the client.
 the client then sends the token back to the server with each request. if the token is not present or is invalid, 
 the server will reject the request.

for file upload we have to add enctype = "multipart/form-data" in form tag otherwise it will not work the image will not be uploaded to the backend

for text data we can use input type = "text" and for file upload we can use input type = "file"

for text data coming from frontened to backend,
request.POST.get("name") 
and for file upload
request.FILES.get("name") 

# to show image to the ui
django managing files.. search and read from documentation
django static files

These settings in settings.py configure how Django handles static files and uploaded media in your project.

STATIC_URL = '/static/'
URL used to access CSS, JavaScript, and other static files.
STATIC_ROOT
Directory where Django collects static files for deployment.
STATICFILES_DIRS
Extra directories where Django looks for static files during development.
MEDIA_ROOT
Directory where uploaded files, such as recipe images, are stored.
MEDIA_URL = '/media/'
URL prefix used to access uploaded images.
in actual application we use cdn to have static files and media files but in development we use local storage to store static and media files.


